week 10:
Last week, I attended a team meeting where we discussed which peripheral modules to include in our RISC-V processor. From this, I chose to work on the TIMER peripheral.
I then researched the TIMER module's functionality. It must include a 48-bit counter running at 25 MHz so that the processor can time how long something takes and delay processes.
It also needs a control register that enables the counter to be stopped, started, and reset. Furthermore, I will have to produce C++ code that can interact with the timer via the FPro bus.
Next, I plan to design the counter and control registers, then use the given testbench to ensure that my TIMER peripheral works as required.
